; pipeline-poke.eval — the one-pipeline check, handed a violation on purpose.
;
; tools\PipelineTest.ps1 -SelfTest runs this and REQUIRES it to report at least
; one violation. Without it, "the pipeline suite passed" could equally mean the
; check had stopped looking — which is the failure every harness in this project
; is built to rule out first (tools\HealthTest.ps1, Bc7Test, AllocTest, Eval).
;
; `pipelinepoke` moves a member's health by a point with no DamageEvent anywhere
; near it: exactly the write the invariant forbids, from a place no game rule
; would ever write from.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11

pipelineguard on
pipelineguard reset

echo === poking health outside the pipeline ===
party
pipelinepoke 0
; One step, so a checkpoint runs and finds it. The poke happens between frames,
; which is what the "outside the world update" checkpoint at the top of
; DungeonWorld::Update is there to cover.
step 1
party
pipeline
state
